# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Vendor SDK binaries (3Brain BioCam Driver API) ---------------------
# Not redistributed here. Copy the DLLs from the 3Brain SDK install into
# BioCam_DupleX_API/API/ and BioCam_DupleX_API/SampleApp_BioCamCL/Dependencies/
*.dll

# --- Recorded data -----------------------------------------------------
# Raw recordings are multi-GB and exceed GitHub's 100 MB file limit, but the
# small per-session JSON beside them is worth versioning. A session leaves
# four files: the .raw, the integrity sidecar, the stimulus log, and the
# session record. The last three are kilobytes and are the only durable
# account of what a run was and what it did - the _session.json in particular,
# which is the one file that says which electrodes were watched, under which
# policy, inside what limits, and whether the run was live or simulated.
#
# The manifest and stimulus log were added in later phases and this rule was
# not updated with them, so they were being ignored while the sidecar was
# kept - versioning the least informative of the three.
# NB: must be "recordings/*" not "recordings/" -- git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so the negations below would never be reached.
*.raw
recordings/*
!recordings/*_meta.json
!recordings/*_session.json
!recordings/*_stimuli.json

# Test fixtures are deliberately committed: small slices of real signal, needed
# to test analysis code on a machine with no instrument.
!tests/fixtures/*.raw

# The UI's demo recording, made by tools/make_demo_recording.py. The .raw is
# already excluded above; the sidecar goes with it. Committing a sidecar
# whose recording is absent is worse than committing neither - it looks like
# a real run that someone forgot to upload.
/demo.raw
/demo_meta.json

